tools-camera-cannot-go = The camera cannot go there
tools-camera-previewing = Camera preview: turn it off to edit
tools-camera-moving = Move to the next keyframe
tools-camera-ease = Ease
tools-camera-help = Drag on the stage to move the camera, or type where it looks. Each change keys the camera at this frame.
tools-help-text = Click the stage and type. Click text to edit it; click away or press Escape to finish.
tools-help-pen = Click for corners, drag for curves. Click the first point to close; Enter or double-click to finish.
tools-help-drag = Drag on the stage.
tools-help-polystar = Drag from the center; the drag sets size and rotation.
tools-help-hand = Drag the stage to pan. Scrolling and middle-drag pan with any tool.
tools-help-zoom = Click to zoom in, Alt-click to zoom out.
tools-help-eyedropper = Click a shape to take its fill; Shift-click takes its stroke.
tools-help-bucket = Click a shape to fill it with the current fill color.
tools-help-ink = Click a shape to outline it with the current stroke.
tools-help-eraser = Click a shape to delete it.
tools-help-pencil = Drag to draw. The line uses the stroke color and width.
tools-help-brush = Drag to paint with the fill color; a pen presses wider.
tools-help-ruler = Drag from one point to another. Points snap to guides, and to the grid when snapping is on.
tools-help-mirror = Click the stage to put the axes there. Pencil and Brush mirror across them.
tools-help-lasso = Drag a loop around shapes to select them; Shift adds to the selection.
tools-help-polygon = Click the corners of a loop around shapes; double-click, Enter or the first corner closes it. Shift adds to the selection.
tools-help-line = Drag on the stage. A line always has a stroke.
tools-help-subselection = Click a shape, then drag its square points to reshape it.
tools-help-add-anchor = Click the outline of a shape to put a point there; the curve keeps its shape.
tools-help-delete-anchor = Click a square point of a shape to take it out; the outline joins across the gap.
tools-help-convert-anchor = Click a curve point to make it a corner; drag from a corner to make it smooth.
tools-help-free-transform = Drag a handle to scale, outside a corner to rotate; Alt on an edge handle skews, Shift keeps proportions.
tools-status-selection = Selection: click to select, drag to move, Shift-click to add
tools-status-subselection = Subselection: click a shape, drag its points
tools-status-add-anchor = Add Anchor Point: click an outline to put a point there
tools-status-delete-anchor = Delete Anchor Point: click a point to remove it
tools-status-convert-anchor = Convert Anchor Point: click for a corner, drag for a smooth point
tools-status-free-transform = Free Transform: drag the handles to scale, rotate or skew
tools-status-rectangle = Rectangle: drag on the stage
tools-status-oval = Oval: drag on the stage
tools-status-line = Line: drag on the stage
tools-status-pen = Pen: click for corners, drag for curves, Enter to finish
tools-status-text = Text: click the stage, type, then Place
tools-status-hand = Hand: drag to pan the stage
tools-status-zoom = Zoom: click to zoom in, Alt-click to zoom out
tools-status-eyedropper = Eyedropper: click a shape to take its color, Shift for the stroke
tools-status-bucket = Paint Bucket: click a shape to fill it
tools-status-ink = Ink Bottle: click a shape to outline it
tools-status-eraser = Eraser: click a shape to delete it
tools-status-polystar = PolyStar: drag from the center
tools-status-lasso = Lasso: drag a loop around shapes to select them
tools-status-polygon = Polygon: click corners, double-click to close and select
tools-status-camera = Camera: drag to move the camera; its controls are in Properties
tools-status-pencil = Pencil: drag to draw
tools-status-brush = Brush: drag to paint
tools-status-ruler = Ruler: drag to measure; Pencil and Brush draw straight with Shift
tools-status-mirror = Mirror: click to set the axes that Pencil and Brush mirror across
tools-status-bone = Bone: drag from one symbol instance to another to link them; pose with the Selection tool
tools-help-bone = Drag from one symbol instance to another to link them with a bone; drag from an instance in an armature to add a bone below it. Pose the armature by dragging its joints with the Selection tool: each pose is a keyframe of the armature layer.
tools-bone-none = Click a joint to set its turn and limits here.
tools-bone-joint = Joint { $number }
tools-bone-turn = Turn
tools-bone-limit = Limit rotation
tools-bone-min = Min
tools-bone-max = Max
tools-bone-detach = Remove bone
tools-bone-release = Release armature
tools-bone-add = Add bone
tools-bone-pose = Pose armature
tools-bone-error = Cannot do that with bones: { $error }
tools-bone-drop-on-instance = A bone ends on a symbol instance: let go over one
